        {
          "id": 2328910234,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The update/setup script ran fine on macos 15.3 with the given versions (ruby, asciidoctor*), so I guess it's OK.\n\n```\nruby 2.6.10p210 (2022-04-12 revision 67958) [universal.arm64e-darwin24]\nASCIIDOCTOR_VERSION=${ASCIIDOCTOR_VERSION-2.0.23}\nASCIIDOCTORPDF_VERSION=${ASCIIDOCTORPDF_VERSION-1.6.1}\n```\n\nThis is not saying that we should stick with an ever older version of Ruby, it's just a \"the patch works for my environment\" statement.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7354663,
            "username": "jmayer2",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jörg Mayer",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/169640aaef0383905a7367726222ac4b97063ae8ad4d0f72aa58ebfe89c33a5d?s=80&d=identicon",
